WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.810
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and tonight is
the season 4 finale.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.029
Because the title is "The Children" I thought
it would be fun to do a video about the Children

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:09.570
of The Forest.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.630
The finale is going to be about a lot of Children.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:15.590
Lannister Children, Stark Children mostly
the people we've been watching all season.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.859
But the Children of the Forest are another
big group of people that the show has mentioned

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:21.080
but not shown visually.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.880
Hello to all the new people, if you're just
now finding me I do weekly Game of Thrones

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.420
videos.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.420
This week is the finale but there's some exciting
stuff happening with A Song of Ice and Fire

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.420
this year.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.420
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.579
I'll talk a little bit more about my plans
going forward tonight in my episode 10 review.

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:40.910
Until then let's start with a history lesson
from Maester Luwin.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.510
May He Rest in Peace.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:45.660
The first time we heard about the Children
of The Forest was during the first book and

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:49.420
season 1 when Bran was listening to stories
from Old Nan and Maester Luwin.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.129
I've always been a fan of the way George RR
Martin gives us history lessons using the

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:56.770
oral tradition just like it would have been
done in the real world before literacy and

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.230
book printing became common.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:01.989
Fun Fact, this year about 10 percent of our
world is still illiterate.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:04.960
That's over 700 million people which is really
depressing.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.880
So a lot of those people just like in A Song
Of Ice and Fire learn history when other people

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:10.880
tell them stories.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:11.880
What are the Children?

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.970
I think the best way to describe them is being
aboriginal Westerosi.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.710
The very first people to inhabit Westeros.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:22.080
They didn't call it Westeros at the time,
but it wasn't till about 12 thousand years

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.150
ago that they made first contact with the
First Men.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.830
Until that time they just lived in symbiosis
with the land.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:32.090
After a prolonged war with the First Men they
signed a pact that gave the First Men the

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:38.770
land that would become modern day Westeros
and the Children took the Forests.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:41.830
So really they never called themselves Children
of The Forest, it's just like the Wildlings

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.130
not thinking of themselves as Wildlings.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:47.000
It's just someone else's term for describing
them.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.490
No one understands the language they spoke,
but it's referred to as being very musical

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:57.360
in nature.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.549
They hunted in groups and used weapons and
implements the way real life Aboriginal people

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:02.549
did.

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:08.590
With a similar social structure.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:12.340
They were the ones that originally used Obsidian
to make their tools.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.910
That's what that Dragonglass dagger was made
of that we saw Samwell use to kill the White

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.130
Walker.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:24.270
Maester Luwin tells Bran that the Children
died a thousand years ago and the only thing

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:29.310
we have left to remember them is the faces
on all the Weirwood trees.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:33.260
Like this face right here.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.750
It's believed that the Children are the ones
that carve the faces into the trees, they

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.629
don't spontaneously grow that way.

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:42.560
I think it's funny that Maester Luwin is totally
convinced that the Children are gone but up

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:48.370
until the season 1 finale all the characters
wouldn't stop talking about how Dragons were

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.849
long dead and gone from the world.

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:53.010
That's one of my favorite things about the
show and the books.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:57.129
It makes you feel like sometimes the characters
are unreliable narrators.

00:02:57.129 --> 00:03:00.730
Like when we're in a POV chapter or a character
on the show is telling a story.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.519
They believe what they're saying is true even
if they might have it wrong.

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:05.480
Dragons being the best example.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:10.200
Even a couple episodes ago before Ser Jorah
ran afoul of Tywin Lannister it seemed like

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:16.840
a lot of people on the small council didn't
believe Daenerys' Dragons were real.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.310
So anytime you hear a legend or a prophecy
like the Children of the Forest, it might

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.310
just be true.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:27.120
They're associated with a couple of the big
world changing events the show has mentioned.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.360
Most notably the Long Night.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.670
But they were also responsible for the shattering
of the arm of Dorne.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:36.299
That's the land bridge that connected Westeros
to Essos the eastern continent.

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:39.810
I remember the first time I heard that all
I could think about was the Isthmus of Panama.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.690
That was a real life land bridge that allowed
a bunch of animals to travel back and forth

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.240
between North and South America during the
Eocene Era.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.450
That was about 56 million years ago.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:55.110
But there have been land bridges connecting
continents that have come and gone as sea

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.110
levels change.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:00.670
In Game of Thrones George RR Martin just uses
magic and war to get rid of that land bridge

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:01.670
in Dorne.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:05.650
About 4 thousand years after their war with
the First Men ended, the White Walkers invaded.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:07.790
That was the beginning of the Long Night.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.569
Based on the way the literature has portrayed
the Children and the White Walkers I choose

00:04:11.569 --> 00:04:17.640
to think of them as the most important two
sides of the Fire and Ice coin.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:21.959
The Children originated the only weapon that's
known to kill White Walkers, the obsidian

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:22.990
blades.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:26.490
We know more about the magic of the White
Walkers than the Children, but as the story

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:30.490
unfolds I think we'll find a lot more similarities.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:35.630
Based on Old Nan's stories, the major hero
of the Long Night, called the last hero, was

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:38.740
only able to defeat the White Walkers with
the help of the Children and their magic.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:46.880
So regardless of which way they come back
into the story, they'll be very important.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:57.430
We do know a big source of their power was
greensight.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:02.310
The ability to see prophetic dreams.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:07.160
On the show Jojen said that Green Dreams always
come true, but it's possible that they could

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.780
be subject to interpretation.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:12.120
Or like in the case of Daenerys and Melisandre's
visions, they could be seeing things that

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.460
may have happened in an alternate timeline.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.990
There's still a lot we don't know about The
Children's power and the White Walkers for

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:18.990
that matter.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:23.990
So I'm really hoping that the future books
and seasons of the show give us more background

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.850
because it definitely goes deeper than Necromancy
and Prophecy Dreams.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:30.590
To be clear though, I don't expect season
5 of the show to completely lay everything

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:31.590
out.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:36.449
I'll talk more about that when I do my predictions
video.

00:05:36.449 --> 00:05:43.380
This season Bran has had a lot of visions
of the great Weirwood in the North.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:47.770
Maester Luwin told him that supposedly, the
faces on those trees allow the Children to

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:50.650
see things wherever there are other weirwoods
with faces.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.870
It reminds me of Professor X inside Cerebro.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.730
It gives him the ability to see all over the
world.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:59.550
Stannis' story is a good example of some weaknesses
to that power.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:03.389
There used to be weirwoods in all of the castles
of westeros, the heart trees like in the godswood

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:04.490
at Winterfell.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:08.479
But when Stannis became a follower of the
Red God, he burned his tree as a symbolic

00:06:08.479 --> 00:06:11.979
way of casting out the old gods and letting
in a new one.

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:19.819
Not to imply that the Red God is a newer god
than the Old Gods.

00:06:19.819 --> 00:06:23.630
The literature isn't really clear about whether
the deities actually exist or if magic comes

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:25.520
from some other place.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:33.539
I know a lot of you guys have theories that
some of the gods are just different aspects

00:06:33.539 --> 00:06:34.990
of the same god.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:38.669
Like saying that the Muslim god and the christian
god are the same thing and both religions

00:06:38.669 --> 00:06:40.870
just interpret it differently.

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:46.949
I don't think that's completely true, but
I do believe that a lot of the smaller prophecies

00:06:46.949 --> 00:06:49.220
are different parts of a larger prophecy.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.830
Without talking too much about tonight's episode,
I'm really hoping we see a teaser for the

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:59.819
Children of The Forest.

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:03.699
Based on the amount of book material the show
has done there's still a lot of Book 4 and

00:07:03.699 --> 00:07:05.210
5 to do next year.

